WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:08.320
A hair cell fails when a gene is missing, and the gene's protein sits in the right

2
00:00:08.320 --> 00:00:11.200
place. Is that enough to call the protein the channel?

3
00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:15.000
A protein can be required for a current without forming the pore.

4
00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:20.500
A trafficking factor, an anchor, or a lipid-modifying enzyme could all be needed.

5
00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:23.120
Deleting any of them would silence the cell.

6
00:00:24.133 --> 00:00:26.353
So the field asks for a ladder of evidence.

7
00:00:26.973 --> 00:00:28.773
Each rung rules out a different alternative.

8
00:00:29.353 --> 00:00:30.813
The first rung is localization.

9
00:00:31.533 --> 00:00:34.913
The protein sits at the lower end of the tip link, where the channel is thought to

10
00:00:34.913 --> 00:00:37.633
be. The next rungs are requirement and rescue.

11
00:00:38.213 --> 00:00:44.013
In neonatal mouse hair cells lacking both TMC1 and TMC2, the conventional current is

12
00:00:44.013 --> 00:00:46.913
gone. Put either gene back, and the current returns.

13
00:00:47.493 --> 00:00:49.213
That puts the proteins in the pathway.

14
00:00:49.213 --> 00:00:52.173
It does not separate a pore from a factor the pore needs.

15
00:00:53.233 --> 00:00:55.613
The next rung changes the protein instead.

16
00:00:56.293 --> 00:00:59.953
The Beethoven mouse carries one altered residue in TMC1.

17
00:01:00.493 --> 00:01:04.973
In excised neonatal mouse inner hair cells, calcium permeability was reduced.

18
00:01:05.713 --> 00:01:07.473
Single-channel size is disputed.

19
00:01:08.113 --> 00:01:11.693
A sequence change that alters which ions pass is strong evidence.

20
00:01:12.433 --> 00:01:16.973
A partner can also change permeation, so this rung is strong but not conclusive.

21
00:01:18.167 --> 00:01:21.647
The accessibility test starts with cells that already carry current.

22
00:01:22.247 --> 00:01:28.407
In mouse hair cells lacking both TMC1 and TMC2, Pan and colleagues delivered TMC1

23
00:01:28.407 --> 00:01:30.107
with a single cysteine substitution.

24
00:01:30.907 --> 00:01:34.487
They added a reagent that cannot cross the membrane and reacts with cysteine in

25
00:01:34.487 --> 00:01:37.727
water. The reagent changed the permeation of the current.

26
00:01:38.267 --> 00:01:43.027
The current existed before the reagent, so altered synthesis or delivery cannot

27
00:01:43.027 --> 00:01:44.067
explain the change.

28
00:01:44.627 --> 00:01:46.527
The cells still had their native partners.

29
00:01:47.700 --> 00:01:53.320
Purified truncated turtle TMC1, in liposomes, responded to applied pressure.

30
00:01:54.060 --> 00:01:57.380
The proteins were not mammalian, and this was not a native complex.

31
00:01:58.120 --> 00:01:59.940
So the answer is a complex of proteins.

32
00:02:00.620 --> 00:02:06.340
In mouse cochlear outer hair cells, TMC1 and TMC2 did not support transduction

33
00:02:06.340 --> 00:02:12.980
without TMIE. Partners such as LHFPL5 and CIB2 change what you measure.

34
00:02:14.033 --> 00:02:16.973
No single paper climbs every rung.

35
00:02:17.073 --> 00:02:21.153
Even a complete ladder says only that the protein forms or lines the pore.

36
00:02:21.673 --> 00:02:24.273
It does not say how force from the tip link reaches it.

37
00:02:24.793 --> 00:02:27.073
Of each experiment, ask what it ruled out.

38
00:02:27.573 --> 00:02:28.853
And ask what it leaves open.
